Flexera understands the value that results from employing a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workforce. We recognize that equity necessitates acknowledging past exclusion and that inclusion requires intentional effort. Our DEI (Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion) council is the driving force behind our commitment to championing policies and practices that foster a welcoming environment for all.

We encourage candidates requiring accommodations to please let us know by emailing careers@flexera.com.

# Senior Analyst - Business Services Team - London

London, United Kingdom

and 1 more

(On-site)

## Job Description

Lazard is one of the world’s leading financial advisory and asset management firms. **Our people make the difference**. With just over 3,000 employees globally, our tight-knit community allows for professionals eager to learn and willing to teach to connect and grow together. We believe that diversity, equity, inclusion, and allyship are not just business imperatives — they are central pillars of our employee experience. Our entrepreneurial culture and flat structure allow creative ideas and original concepts to drive our business forward — and for careers to take flight.

Through our financial advisory business, Lazard advises clients around the world on strategic and financial matters including mergers and acquisitions, restructurings, capital structure and capital raising. Our client relationships are built on trust and discretion. As the world’s largest advisory-focused firm, we have exceptional depth of expertise across industry sectors and geographies. We value the rich diversity that comes from blending local perspective with our global network.

**Senior Analyst – Business Services M&A Team – London**

Lazard is seeking to recruit an Associate to join the Business Services M&A Team in London.

The Senior Analyst will report to senior bankers on each transaction.  You will be responsible for the day-to-day support of marketing efforts and transaction execution and have a central role on client interactions. The Senior Analyst will contribute to the team’s collegial culture, with a focus on collaboration and talent development. We are looking for a proactive, enthusiastic and motivated individual, with at least 1-2 years M&A experience, to join the team in London.

**We’ll trust you to:**

* Demonstrate strong technical and analytical skills with an ability to build financial models;
* Research, analyse, sensitise and adapt both internal and client-facing financial and statistical analysis/ models;
* Efficiently evaluate qualitative and quantitative data;
* Be responsible for assisting in the preparation and production of presentations and marketing materials for clients and prospective clients, in consultation with other team members;
* Assist MDs and senior bankers on an ad hoc basis as needed with various reports and analyses;
* Assist in due diligence efforts as appropriate;
* Use your own knowledge and judgement to add information to presentations where appropriate;
* Identify issues arising and offer potential solutions
* Communicate effectively and appropriately;
* Turn ideas into concise and comprehensive presentations;
* Be a proactive team participant with a natural ability to develop their profile across Lazard groups and regions;
* Anticipate needs and be proactive in making value-added contributions;
* Independently develop sound and logical views whilst understanding both the big picture and the minutiae;
* Show confidence, professionalism and accountability at all times;
* Contribute to firm-wide initiatives including recruiting, training and professional development.

**You’ll need to have:**

* Gained relevant M&A experience within an investment banking environment. Previous M&A transaction experience would be helpful but is not essential;
* Robust understanding of the accounting principles that underlie typical financial analyses used in advisory (particularly valuation);
* Outstanding financial understanding that can be readily translated into modelling that is used for both marketing and execution purposes;
* Self-motivation, with demonstrable ability to manage conflicting priorities and requests in a high pressure environment;
* The ability to take initiative and function independently, balanced with strong team skills;
* Excellent interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to maintain relationships with colleagues and clients at all levels;
* Strong verbal and written communication skills;
* The ability to deliver requested materials to senior bankers in a timely manner;
* Fluency with AI tools and emerging technologies to enhance analysis, research and workflow efficiency while maintaining a high quality and integrity of output;
* The skills to maintain high standards of professional and ethical conduct, adhere to legal and regulatory requirements of the banking environment and follow Lazard policies and procedures;
* Minimum 2.1 university degree classification (or equivalent if studied outside the UK);

**What we offer**

We strive to enhance the total health and well-being of our employees through comprehensive, competitive benefits. Our goal is to offer a highly individualized employee experience that enables you to balance your commitments to career, family, and community. When you work for Lazard, you are working for an organization that cares about your unique talents and passions, and will continue to invest in the development of your career.

**Does this sound like you?**

Apply! We’ll get in touch on the next steps.

**Representation at Lazard**

Lazard is an intellectual capital business committed to delivering the best advice and solutions to clients. To achieve these objectives, we focus on attracting, developing and retaining the best talent. We believe that a workforce comprised of people who represent a wide array of backgrounds, experiences and perspectives creates a rich variety of thought that empowers us to challenge conventional wisdom, solve problems creatively and make better decisions.

Lazard was built on the premise that a multicultural firm can best serve a global clientele. As a global firm that has grown organically from local roots in different countries, we have a deep tradition of respecting and appreciating individual differences. Doing so has been core to our success for over 175 years. We are committed to sustaining an environment where every colleague is supported in their professional pursuits, can maximize their individual potential and contribute to our collective success.

#LI-HB1

## Principal Project Controller

Apply

:   GB - Edinburgh
:   GB - Luton - Cap. Green 300

:   Full time

:   Posted Today

:   R0033103

**Job Description:**

**Your Impact**

We are looking for an experienced Principal Project Controller to work with our Bids and Proposals team within CS3. The CS3 Project Controls team is undergoing an exciting transformation in our ways of working - this is a high visibility opportunity to work across our Sectors and to embed good practices early in the project lifecycle. This role is hybrid with the expectation of at least **2 days on-site.**

**What you'll do as a Bids and Proposals Principal Project Controller**:

* Develop the Work Breakdown Structure in conjunction with the Project or Bid Manager and relevant functional stakeholders;
* Facilitate planning workshops with work package owners and functional contributors;
* Create and maintain fit-for-purpose schedules in Primavera P6 by defining activities, milestones, durations, logic, constraints, calendars and coding in accordance with applicable Leonardo and CS3 standards;
* Produce schedule extracts and visualisations appropriate for Business Winning Reviews, Tender Vet, Phase Reviews and management reviews;
* Support or perform Schedule Risk Analysis where required by the scale, risk and maturity of the opportunity.

**What You'll Bring**

* Comprehensive and demonstrable Project Controls/ Planning experience with proven expertise in all aspects of planning, project controls and project management methodologies (inc AGILE) across Projects of  varying value/complexity;
* Expertise in one or more Planning/ERP Tools (ideally including Primavera P6 and/or SAP);
* Breadth of experience in all parts of lifecycle and experience in the phases of initiation, planning and execution;
* Proven collaboration, communication, planning, problem solving, decision making skills;
* Application of Schedule Risk Analysis including identification, methods of analysis and recommendations for management;
* Commercial and financial acumen;
* APMG Project Controls Foundation and Practitioner Level Certification or meet the criteria to undertake this training;
* Ability to engage and influence cross-functional teams and recognise and positively interact with stakeholders up to VP level;
* Experience of coaching, mentoring or team leadership.

**Security Clearance**

This role is subject to pre-employment screening in line with the UK Government’s Baseline Personnel Security Standard (BPSS). An additional range of Personnel Security Controls referred to as National Security Vetting (NSV) may apply, this could include meeting the eligibility requirements for The Security Check (SC) or Developed Vetting (DV). For more information and guidance please visit: https://careers.uk.leonardo.com/gb/en/security-and-vetting

**Why Join Us**

At Leonardo, our people are at the heart of everything we do. We offer a comprehensive, company-funded benefits package that supports your wellbeing, career development, and work–life balance. Whether you're looking to grow professionally, care for your health, or plan for the future, we’re here to help you thrive.

* Time to Recharge: Enjoy generous leave with the opportunity to accrue up to 12 additional flexidays each year;
* Secure your Future: Benefit from our award-winning pension scheme with up to 15% employer contribution;
* Your Wellbeing Matters: Free access to mental health support, financial advice, and employee-led networks championing inclusion and diversity (Enable, Pride, Equalise, Armed Forces, Carers,  Wellbeing and Ethnicity);
* Rewarding Performance: All employees at management level and below are eligible for our bonus scheme;
* Never Stop Learning: Free access to 4,000+ online courses via Coursera and LinkedIn Learning;
* Refer a friend: Receive a financial reward through our referral programme;
* Tailored Perks: Spend up to £500 annually on flexible benefits including private healthcare, dental, family cover, tech & lifestyle discounts, gym memberships and more;
* Flexible working: Flexible hours with hybrid working options. For part time opportunities, please talk to us about what might be possible for this role.

For a full list of our company benefits please visit our website.

Leonardo UK operates a grade-based salary framework with broad bands. The salary range shown reflects the approved grade band for this role, or a narrower hiring range published within that band, and is benchmarked against the external market. Exceptions above the standard range are managed through governance controls to protect internal equity.

Leonardo is a global leader in Aerospace, Defence, and Security. Headquartered in Italy, we employ over 53,000 people worldwide including 8,500 across 9 sites in the UK. Our employees are not just part of a team—they are key contributors to shaping innovation, advancing technology, and enhancing global safety.

At Leonardo we are committed to building an inclusive, accessible, and welcoming workplace. We believe that a diverse workforce sparks creativity, drives innovation, and leads to better outcomes for our people and our customers. If you have any accessibility requirements to support you during the recruitment  process, just let us know.

Be part of something bigger - apply now!

**Primary Location:**

GB - Edinburgh

**Additional Locations:**

GB - Luton - Cap. Green 300

**Contract Type:**

Permanent

**Hybrid Working:**

Hybrid

Do you have an eye for beautiful design, a passion for flowers, and love bringing creative ideas to life?

Rocket Food is looking for an experienced Junior Florist and Creative Designer to join our talented team. This is a hands-on, sometimes client-facing role where no two days are the same. From creating stunning floral installations and styling luxury tastings to transforming event spaces and keeping our shopfront looking exceptional, you’ll play a key role in delivering the creativity, quality and attention to detail that define Rocket Food.

**The Role**- Styling and maintaining the front-of-house Rocket Food shopfront aesthetic, including reception areas, tasting rooms and client-facing spaces.  
- Ensuring it is seasonal, inspiring and consistently reflects the company's brand and ethos;  
- Producing creative concepts, mood boards, quotations and floral proposals for clients and events;  
- Designing and creating bespoke floral arrangements for tastings and events;  
- Creating seasonal canapé tray designs and innovative food presentation concepts that enhance the client experience and maintain our reputation for innovative design;  
- Developing creative table-to-table (T2T) styling and presentation concepts that complement Rocket Food's catering and event experiences;  
- Supporting the wider events team with the installation, styling and breakdown of event décor and displays as required;  
- Working closely with the Sales, Events and Kitchen teams to develop creative solutions for client briefs and event concepts;  
- Building positive relationships with clients, suppliers and colleagues, providing a professional and consultative service throughout the design process.

- Managing floral stock, materials and props, ensuring efficient ordering, storage and quality control;  
- Staying up-to-date with seasonal trends, floristry techniques and design innovations, bringing fresh ideas to the business;  
- Ensuring all work is delivered on time, within budget and to Rocket Food's exceptionally-high standards of creativity and presentation.

**About You - you'll be:**- A florist with excellent design, styling skills;  
- Naturally creative with a strong eye for colour, detail and presentation;  
- Confident working directly with clients and understanding their vision;  
- Happy working both independently and as part of a collaborative and creative team;  
- Organised, proactive and able to manage multiple projects;  
- Comfortable with early starts, event installations and working in a fast-paced environment;  
- Passionate about creating memorable experiences through flowers and design;  
- Ideally, a driver.

**Why Rocket Food?**  
At Rocket Food, creativity is at the heart of everything we do. From extraordinary events to beautifully styled tastings, we're known for delivering exceptional food and unforgettable experiences. If you love design, thrive on variety, and want to see your work enjoyed by some of London's most exciting clients, we'd love to hear from you.

**Interested?**  
